In terms of size, the Scarlet Tanager is approximately 7-8 inches long, with a wingspan of about 10-11 inches. It is a relatively large songbird compared to many other species.

Behaviorally, the Scarlet Tanager is primarily a forest-dwelling bird, often found in deciduous forests and woodlands. It is known for its loud, melodious song, which can be heard during the breeding season. The bird is also territorial and will defend its nesting area vigorously.

The Scarlet Tanager is easily identifiable by its bright red coloration, black wingtips, and distinctive song. Its size and shape also help to distinguish it from other similar birds.
